---
title: Sheet Pan Cashew Chicken
description: A quick weeknight sheet pan dinner of tender chicken and vegetables tossed with roasted cashews in a savory-sweet Asian-inspired sauce.
course: main
cuisine: Asian American
servings: 4
time required: 25 minutes
prep time: 5 minutes
cook time: 20 minutes
source: https://therecipecritic.com/sheet-pan-cashew-chicken/
image: https://therecipecritic.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/04/Sheet-Pan-Cashew-Chicken-1-e1491914260409.jpg
tags:
  - chicken
  - sheet pan
  - weeknight
  - asian
---

In a medium #saucepan{} over medium heat, whisk together @low-sodium soy sauce{6%tablespoons}, @hoisin sauce{1%tablespoon}, @apple cider vinegar{3/4%tablespoon}, @honey{2%tablespoons}, @toasted sesame oil{1%teaspoon}, @fresh ginger{1/2%teaspoon}(minced), @garlic{2%teaspoons}(minced), @cornstarch{2%tablespoons}, and @water{1/2%cup} until combined.

Bring to a simmer, stirring frequently, until the sauce thickens and bubbles ~{2-3%minutes}. Remove from heat and set aside.

Preheat the #oven{} to 400F. Line a large #sheet pan{} with parchment paper and set aside.

Season @chicken breasts{1%pound}(boneless, skinless, cut into 1-inch cubes) with @salt and @pepper. Place on the pan and drizzle with half the sauce; reserve the rest for later.

Cook the chicken in the preheated oven ~oven{8%minutes}, then remove the pan.

Arrange @broccoli florets{1 1/2%cups}, @red bell pepper{1}(chopped), @green bell pepper{1}(chopped), and @roasted unsalted cashews{2/3%cup} around the chicken in a single layer. Drizzle with spoonfuls of sauce and toss to coat. Return to the oven and cook ~oven{8-12%minutes} more, or until the chicken is cooked through and the juices run clear.

Remove from oven and drizzle with the remaining sauce. Serve over rice or quinoa and garnish with @toasted sesame seeds{} and @green onions{}(chopped), if desired.
